 "summary": "Spherical Bessel functions are absent from Mathlib (no `Bessel` match anywhere in `./mathlib`), and each of the four new general-purpose lemmas fills a verified upstream gap: no `AnalyticAt`/`AnalyticOnNhd` statement about `dslope` exists, no `Function.Even.deriv`, and Mathlib's `Sinc.lean` has neither analyticity nor `x * sinc x = sin x`. The construction reuses the located upstream API where it can (`sub_smul_dslope`, `dslope_eventuallyEq_slope_of_ne`, `HasFPowerSeriesAt.has_fpower_series_dslope_fslope`, `sinc_eq_dslope`, `Function.Odd.map_zero`, `deriv_comp_neg`, `Nat.doubleFactorial_add_two`), and each helper has a real consumer in the Bessel file.",
